<Docs title="Connect Grok — Botpasses" crumbs={[{ href: "/docs", label: "Docs" }, { href: "/docs/connect/grok", label: "Grok" }]}>
  <h1>Connect Grok</h1>
  <p>
    The supported Grok path is this origin’s <code>/mcp</code> URL plus
    <code>Authorization: Bearer avm_…</code>. Issue the token from the Access panel
    (<code>POST /api/clients/model</code>). Grok adds the Bearer scheme. That header is
    enough. <code>initialize</code>, <code>tools/list</code>, and <code>http.request</code>
    work without an OAuth connect card and without <code>needsAuth</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not paste an operator token, a Client Secret, or a third-party JWT into Grok.
    The model never sees vault values.
  </p>

  <h2>OAuth connect cards</h2>
  <p>
    If Grok (or Cursor) starts Dynamic Client Registration, Botpasses accepts
    <code>https</code>, loopback <code>http://127.0.0.1</code>, and desktop app schemes
    such as <code>cursor://</code> and <code>grok://</code>. A connect card still fails
    if the client sends a blocked scheme (<code>javascript:</code>, <code>data:</code>,
    <code>file:</code>). Prefer the <code>avm_</code> header. You do not need to complete
    the card when Bearer is already configured.
  </p>

  <h2>Spotify</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A Client Secret is not a user access token. Do not inject it as <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> on <code>api.spotify.com</code>.</li>
    <li>Token mint is <code>POST https://accounts.spotify.com/api/token</code> with HTTP Basic (<code>client_id:client_secret</code>) and <code>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</code> body <code>grant_type=client_credentials</code>. JSON + Bearer of the secret is invalid.</li>
    <li>Store the secret as inject <code>client_credentials</code> (or pass public <code>client_id</code> on <code>http.request</code>). Botpasses mints and caches an app token, then calls <code>api.spotify.com</code>. The access token is redacted in the tool result.</li>
    <li><code>GET /v1/search</code> works with that app token. <code>GET /v1/me</code> and private playlist writes need Authorization Code + PKCE. Use <strong>Connect Spotify user</strong> on the vault item. Redirect is this origin’s <code>/integrations/spotify/callback</code> or <code>http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback</code>. Add that URI on the Spotify app. The refresh token stays in the vault.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Grants</h2>
  <p>
    Grant policy <code>prompt</code> is one successful inject. A failed origin HTTP
    (401/410) does not consume the approve. Retry <code>http.request</code> with the
    same item, host, method, and path. Do not ask for a new 8-digit code after a failed
    Spotify call. Approve in the inbox; the page says the agent can retry.
  </p>
  <p>Tool contract: <a href="/docs/reference/mcp-tools">MCP tools</a>. Issue the model Bearer from the console or via <a href="/docs/reference/http-api">POST /api/clients/model</a>.</p>
</Docs>
